  "stem": "What is the solution to the equation \\(|x - 3| = 2x\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "1"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Case 1: \\(x - 3 = 2x\\) gives \\(x = -3\\). Check: \\(|-6| = 6\\), but \\(2(-3) = -6\\), so \\(-3\\) is not a solution.",
    "Case 2: \\(x - 3 = -2x\\) gives \\(3x = 3\\), so \\(x = 1\\). Check: \\(|-2| = 2 = 2(1)\\).",
    "The only solution is \\(1\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "x = symbols('x', real=True)\nsol = solve(Eq(Abs(x - 3), 2*x), x)\nassert sol == [1]\nassert [Rational(s) for s in spr_answers] == sol",
